    relatedNodes: ["dunya", "hamm", "sadaqa"],
    thesis: "What a person really owns is only what he used up or gave away. The rest belongs to his heirs. Whoever makes the world his biggest concern is tied to endless worry, work, need and hope. What the world offers ends as bones and rags.",
    context: "Ghazali continues the reports from the Prophet and the earlier prophets. He moves from the world's worth to what it does to the heart that makes it its main concern.",
    moves: [
      { title: "My wealth, my wealth", body: "The Prophet recited: “Competing for more distracts you.” Then he said: “The son of Adam says: my wealth, my wealth. But do you own any of your wealth except what you ate and used up, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and so kept?” It is also reported: when God sent Adam down to earth, He told him: “Build for ruin, and give birth for death.”" },
      { title: "A home for the homeless", body: "The Prophet said: “The world is the home of one who has no home, and the wealth of one who has no wealth. The one with no sense gathers for it. The one with no knowledge makes enemies over it. The one with no understanding envies for it. And the one with no certainty strives for it.”" },
      { title: "Four things for ever", body: "The Prophet said: “Whoever wakes up with the world as his biggest concern has nothing to do with God. God binds four things to his heart. A worry that never leaves him. A busyness he is never free of. A poverty that never reaches wealth. And a hope that never reaches its end.”" },
      { title: "The valley of heads", body: "Abu Hurayra said the messenger of God told him: “Abu Hurayra, shall I show you the whole world and everything in it?” He said yes. The Prophet took him by the hand to a valley near Medina. There was a rubbish heap with human skulls, filth, rags and bones. He said: “Abu Hurayra, these heads were greedy like your greed and hoped like your hope. Today they are bones without skin, and they will become ash. This filth was their many kinds of food. They earned it however they earned it, then filled their bellies with it. Now people keep away from it. These worn-out rags were their fine clothes; now the winds toss them. These bones are the bones of the animals they rode to the ends of the land. Whoever would weep over the world should weep.” Abu Hurayra said: “We did not leave until we were weeping hard.”" },
      { title: "Abraham's scrolls", body: "Dawud ibn Hilal said it is written in the scrolls of Abraham: “World, how worthless you are to the righteous, for whom you dressed up! I have put hatred of you and turning from you into their hearts. I created nothing more worthless to Me than you. Everything about you is small and heading for ruin. On the day I made you, I decreed that you would last for no one. And no one would last for you, even if your owner is stingy with you. Blessed are the righteous, who showed Me contentment in their hearts and truthfulness in their minds. When they come to Me from their graves, their reward is light running before them. Angels will surround them until I bring them to the mercy they hoped for.”" },
      { title: "The world asks for a share", body: "The Prophet said: “The world hangs between heaven and earth. God has not looked at it since He created it. On the Day of Resurrection it will say: Lord, give me to the lowest of Your friends as his share today. He will say: Be quiet, you nothing. I was not pleased to give you to them in the world. Would I be pleased to give you to them today?”" },
      { title: "Adam and the one tree", body: "A story is told about Adam. When he ate from the tree, his stomach stirred with the need to relieve himself. None of the foods of the Garden did that except this tree; that was why he and Eve had been forbidden it. Adam began wandering about the Garden. God told an angel to ask him what he wanted. Adam said he wanted to empty his stomach of its waste. The angel was told to say: “Where do you want to put it? On the carpets, the couches, the rivers, or under the shade of the trees? Do you see any place here fit for that? Go down to the world.”" },
    ],
